{"id":"p07-l11","minutes":40,"summary":"A magnetometer gives heading from the Earth’s field, until nearby steel and magnets distort it. You model hard-iron offsets and soft-iron distortion, fit an ellipsoid to readings taken while tumbling the device, map it back to a sphere, and get heading within 2 degrees.","html":"<h2 id=\"heading-from-the-earth-s-field\">Heading from the Earth’s field</h2>\n<p>The Earth’s field is 25–65 µT, with a horizontal component pointing to magnetic north and a vertical component (the <em>inclination</em>) pointing down in the northern hemisphere. With the device level, the heading is</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8889em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">ψ</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0361em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">atan2</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>When tilted, first rotate the reading into the horizontal plane using roll and pitch from the accelerometer (lesson 9): a <em>tilt-compensated compass</em>.</p>\n<h2 id=\"hard-and-soft-iron\">Hard and soft iron</h2>\n<p>Mounted in a robot, the sensor sees more than the Earth:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Hard iron</strong>: permanent magnets and magnetised steel add a constant vector <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">h</span></span></span></span> that rotates with the device. It shifts the sphere of readings off-centre.</li>\n<li><strong>Soft iron</strong>: nearby ferrous material bends the field, so the readings are a linear map <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span> of the true field. It stretches the sphere into an ellipsoid.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5944em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7667em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">m</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7778em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">h</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6679em;\"></span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">noise</span></span><span class=\"mord\">.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<h2 id=\"ellipsoid-fit\">Ellipsoid fit</h2>\n<p>Tumble the device through many orientations. The true field has constant magnitude, so the raw readings lie on an ellipsoid:</p>\n<div class=\"math-scroll\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.1491em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">h</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8991em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.113em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">⊤</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">h</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1.</span></span></span></span></span></div>\n<p>Expanding gives an equation that is <strong>linear</strong> in 9 unknowns (6 for the symmetric quadratic part, 3 for the linear part), which least squares solves (lesson 2). From the fit:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Centre <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">h</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.0085em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">1</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\" style=\"margin-right:0.016em;\">g</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Shape: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mord\">/</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span></span></span></span> with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0315em;\">k</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">h</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8491em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">⊤</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">A</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">h</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Correction: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.4444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">m</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1.138em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.109em;\">M</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.888em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">1/2</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathbf\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0278em;\">r</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">a</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0269em;\">w</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbf\">h</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, which puts the readings back on a sphere of radius <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0502em;\">B</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n</ol>\n\n<figure class=\"fig\"><div class=\"fig-body\"><div class=\"widget\" data-widget=\"magcal\" data-args=\"{}\"></div></div><figcaption>Readings while turning a full circle, level. Hard iron shifts the circle, soft iron stretches it; turn on the calibration to map it back.</figcaption></figure>\n<h2 id=\"worked-example\">Worked example</h2>\n<p>A level robot reads <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.5806em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">x</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6444em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">37</span></span></span></span> µT, <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7167em;vertical-align:-0.2861em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">m</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1514em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"katex-sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0359em;\">y</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.2861em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.7278em;vertical-align:-0.0833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">23</span></span></span></span> µT. The calibration found a hard-iron offset of (15, −8) µT and no soft iron.</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Raw heading: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">atan2</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">23</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">37</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">31.9°</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>Corrected: <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">37</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">−</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.8389em;vertical-align:-0.1944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">15</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">23</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">8</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">22</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">15</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, so <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">atan2</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">15</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">22</span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">=</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"katex-base\"><span class=\"katex-strut\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">34.3°</span></span></span></span>.</li>\n<li>The offset caused a 2.4° error at this heading. It’s worse at other headings: for a 20 µT horizontal field, a 17 µT offset can cause errors of tens of degrees.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"code-it-from-scratch\">Code it from scratch</h2>\n\n<div class=\"code-card\" data-code=\"0\"><div class=\"code-head\"><span class=\"fname\" translate=\"no\">mag_calibration.py</span><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-copy=\"0\">Copy</button><button class=\"btn btn-quiet btn-small\" type=\"button\" data-download=\"0\">Download</button></div><pre tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-python\"><span class=\"hljs-keyword\">import</span> numpy <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">as</span> np\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(<span class=\"hljs-number\">12</span>)\nB_WORLD = np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">20.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">40.0</span>])                       <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># µT: north and down (x north, z up)</span>\nS = np.array([[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.25</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.10</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.02</span>], [<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.10</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.90</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span>], [<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.02</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.05</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.05</span>]])   <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># symmetric soft iron</span>\nH = np.array([<span class=\"hljs-number\">15.0</span>, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">8.0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">22.0</span>])                              <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># hard iron</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">rot</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">yaw, pitch, roll</span>):\n    cy, sy, cp, sp, cr, sr = np.cos(yaw), np.sin(yaw), np.cos(pitch), np.sin(pitch), np.cos(roll), np.sin(roll)\n    Rz = np.array([[cy, -sy, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], [sy, cy, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], [<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>]])\n    Ry = np.array([[cp, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, sp], [<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], [-sp, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, cp]])\n    Rx = np.array([[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], [<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, cr, -sr], [<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, sr, cr]])\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> Rz @ Ry @ Rx                                          <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># body -&gt; world</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">read</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">R</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> S @ (R.T @ B_WORLD) + H + <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.3</span> * rng.standard_normal(<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>)\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">fit_ellipsoid</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">P</span>):\n    x, y, z = P.T\n    D = np.column_stack([x*x, y*y, z*z, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>*x*y, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>*x*z, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>*y*z, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>*x, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>*y, <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>*z])\n    p = np.linalg.lstsq(D, np.ones(<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">len</span>(P)), rcond=<span class=\"hljs-literal\">None</span>)[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]\n    A = np.array([[p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>], p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>], p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>]], [p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">3</span>], p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>]], [p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">4</span>], p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>], p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>]]])\n    g = p[<span class=\"hljs-number\">6</span>:]\n    h = -np.linalg.solve(A, g)\n    M = A / (<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span> + h @ A @ h)\n    w, V = np.linalg.eigh(M)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> h, V @ np.diag(np.sqrt(w)) @ V.T                     <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># centre and M^(1/2)</span>\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">def</span> <span class=\"hljs-title function_\">heading</span>(<span class=\"hljs-params\">m</span>):\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">return</span> np.degrees(np.arctan2(-m[<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>], m[<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>]))\n\n<span class=\"hljs-keyword\">if</span> __name__ == <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;__main__&quot;</span>:\n    samples = np.array([read(rot(*rng.uniform([-np.pi, -<span class=\"hljs-number\">1.2</span>, -np.pi], [np.pi, <span class=\"hljs-number\">1.2</span>, np.pi]))) <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> _ <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">range</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">400</span>)])\n    h, Mh = fit_ellipsoid(samples)\n    Bmag = np.linalg.norm(B_WORLD)\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;hard iron estimate:&quot;</span>, h.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">round</span>(<span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span>))\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.allclose(h, H, atol=<span class=\"hljs-number\">0.5</span>)\n    radii = np.linalg.norm((samples - h) @ Mh.T, axis=<span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> np.<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(radii - <span class=\"hljs-number\">1</span>).<span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>() &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.03</span>                       <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># back on the unit sphere</span>\n    worst_raw = worst_cal = <span class=\"hljs-number\">0.0</span>\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">for</span> yaw <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">in</span> np.radians(np.arange(<span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">360</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">5</span>)):                 <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># level headings</span>\n        raw = read(rot(yaw, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>, <span class=\"hljs-number\">0</span>))\n        cal = Bmag * Mh @ (raw - h)\n        true = np.degrees(yaw)\n        wrap = <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">lambda</span> a: (a + <span class=\"hljs-number\">180</span>) % <span class=\"hljs-number\">360</span> - <span class=\"hljs-number\">180</span>\n        worst_raw = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(worst_raw, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(wrap(heading(raw) - true)))\n        worst_cal = <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">max</span>(worst_cal, <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">abs</span>(wrap(heading(cal) - true)))\n    <span class=\"hljs-built_in\">print</span>(<span class=\"hljs-string\">f&quot;worst level heading error: raw <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{worst_raw:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.1</span>f}</span> deg, calibrated <span class=\"hljs-subst\">{worst_cal:<span class=\"hljs-number\">.2</span>f}</span> deg&quot;</span>)\n    <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">assert</span> worst_cal &lt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">2</span> <span class=\"hljs-keyword\">and</span> worst_raw &gt; <span class=\"hljs-number\">20</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2 id=\"exercises\">Exercises</h2>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>Why must you tumble the device in 3D, not just spin it flat, for a full ellipsoid fit?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>A flat spin only samples one slice of the ellipsoid, so the fit can’t determine the vertical offset or the shape along the other axes. The least-squares problem becomes ill-conditioned.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n\n<div class=\"exercise\"><div class=\"ex-q\"><p>A motor current changes the field near the sensor. Can a one-time calibration fix that?</p>\n</div><details><summary>Show the solution</summary><div class=\"ex-s\"><p>No. Calibration fixes constant hard iron and linear soft iron. A current-dependent field varies in time: move the sensor away, or model the disturbance against the measured current.</p>\n</div></details></div>\n<h2 id=\"quiz\">Quiz</h2>\n\n<div class=\"quiz\" data-quiz=\"p07-l11\"></div>\n\n","toc":[{"id":"heading-from-the-earth-s-field","title":"Heading from the Earth’s field"},{"id":"hard-and-soft-iron","title":"Hard and soft iron"},{"id":"ellipsoid-fit","title":"Ellipsoid fit"},{"id":"worked-example","title":"Worked example"},{"id":"code-it-from-scratch","title":"Code it from scratch"},{"id":"exercises","title":"Exercises"},{"id":"quiz","title":"Quiz"}],"quiz":[{"id":"p07-l11-q1","type":"num","q":"<p>Raw heading in degrees for m_x = 37 µT, m_y = −23 µT?</p>\n","explain":"<p>atan2(−m_y, m_x).</p>\n","answer":31.866,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l11-q2","type":"num","q":"<p>Corrected heading in degrees after removing an offset of (15, −8) µT?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Subtract the offset first.</p>\n","answer":34.287,"tol":0.002,"unit":"°"},{"id":"p07-l11-q3","type":"mc","q":"<p>Hard iron…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A constant offset vector.</p>\n","options":["stretches the sphere of readings","shifts its centre","rotates the Earth’s field","adds noise"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l11-q4","type":"mc","q":"<p>Soft iron turns the sphere of readings into…</p>\n","explain":"<p>A linear map.</p>\n","options":["a shifted sphere","an ellipsoid","a plane","a line"],"answer":1},{"id":"p07-l11-q5","type":"num","q":"<p>Unknowns in the linear ellipsoid fit?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Six quadratic and three linear terms.</p>\n","answer":9,"tol":0.001,"unit":""},{"id":"p07-l11-q6","type":"num","q":"<p>Magnitude in µT of a field of (20, 0, −40) µT?</p>\n","explain":"<p>Typical for mid-latitudes.</p>\n","answer":44.721,"tol":0.002,"unit":"µT"}],"code":[{"file":"mag_calibration.py","lang":"python","src":"import numpy as np\n\nrng = np.random.default_rng(12)\nB_WORLD = np.array([20.0, 0.0, -40.0])                       # µT: north and down (x north, z up)\nS = np.array([[1.25, 0.10, 0.02], [0.10, 0.90, -0.05], [0.02, -0.05, 1.05]])   # symmetric soft iron\nH = np.array([15.0, -8.0, 22.0])                              # hard iron\n\ndef rot(yaw, pitch, roll):\n    cy, sy, cp, sp, cr, sr = np.cos(yaw), np.sin(yaw), np.cos(pitch), np.sin(pitch), np.cos(roll), np.sin(roll)\n    Rz = np.array([[cy, -sy, 0], [sy, cy, 0], [0, 0, 1]])\n    Ry = np.array([[cp, 0, sp], [0, 1, 0], [-sp, 0, cp]])\n    Rx = np.array([[1, 0, 0], [0, cr, -sr], [0, sr, cr]])\n    return Rz @ Ry @ Rx                                          # body -> world\n\ndef read(R):\n    return S @ (R.T @ B_WORLD) + H + 0.3 * rng.standard_normal(3)\n\ndef fit_ellipsoid(P):\n    x, y, z = P.T\n    D = np.column_stack([x*x, y*y, z*z, 2*x*y, 2*x*z, 2*y*z, 2*x, 2*y, 2*z])\n    p = np.linalg.lstsq(D, np.ones(len(P)), rcond=None)[0]\n    A = np.array([[p[0], p[3], p[4]], [p[3], p[1], p[5]], [p[4], p[5], p[2]]])\n    g = p[6:]\n    h = -np.linalg.solve(A, g)\n    M = A / (1 + h @ A @ h)\n    w, V = np.linalg.eigh(M)\n    return h, V @ np.diag(np.sqrt(w)) @ V.T                     # centre and M^(1/2)\n\ndef heading(m):\n    return np.degrees(np.arctan2(-m[1], m[0]))\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    samples = np.array([read(rot(*rng.uniform([-np.pi, -1.2, -np.pi], [np.pi, 1.2, np.pi]))) for _ in range(400)])\n    h, Mh = fit_ellipsoid(samples)\n    Bmag = np.linalg.norm(B_WORLD)\n    print(\"hard iron estimate:\", h.round(2))\n    assert np.allclose(h, H, atol=0.5)\n    radii = np.linalg.norm((samples - h) @ Mh.T, axis=1)\n    assert np.abs(radii - 1).max() < 0.03                       # back on the unit sphere\n    worst_raw = worst_cal = 0.0\n    for yaw in np.radians(np.arange(0, 360, 5)):                 # level headings\n        raw = read(rot(yaw, 0, 0))\n        cal = Bmag * Mh @ (raw - h)\n        true = np.degrees(yaw)\n        wrap = lambda a: (a + 180) % 360 - 180\n        worst_raw = max(worst_raw, abs(wrap(heading(raw) - true)))\n        worst_cal = max(worst_cal, abs(wrap(heading(cal) - true)))\n    print(f\"worst level heading error: raw {worst_raw:.1f} deg, calibrated {worst_cal:.2f} deg\")\n    assert worst_cal < 2 and worst_raw > 20"}]}